# Testing Standards

## Test Organization

```
backend/tests/
  conftest.py          — shared fixtures (db session, test client, mock services)
  unit/                — isolated tests, no external deps
    test_config.py
    test_text_normalization.py
    test_chunking.py
    test_similarity.py
    test_schemas.py
  integration/         — tests with real DB/Qdrant (via Docker)
    test_document_pipeline.py
    test_query_pipeline.py
    test_vector_storage.py
    test_database_crud.py
  api/                 — HTTP endpoint tests via TestClient
    test_documents_api.py
    test_queries_api.py
    test_admin_api.py
    test_health_api.py
  e2e/                 — full stack tests
    test_upload_query_flow.py

frontend/rag-ui-new/src/
  __tests__/           — or colocated *.test.tsx next to components
```

## Backend Test Patterns

- Use `@pytest.mark.unit`, `@pytest.mark.integration`, `@pytest.mark.e2e` markers
- Use fixtures for database sessions (`db_session`), test client (`client`), mock services
- Use factories for creating test data (documents, chunks, embeddings)
- Test the data pipeline: extraction -> normalization -> chunking -> embedding -> storage
- Assert on data consistency between PostgreSQL and Qdrant after pipeline runs
- Use `pytest-cov` with `--cov-fail-under=80` for new code

## Frontend Test Patterns

- Use Vitest + React Testing Library + jsdom
- Test component rendering, user interactions, and API integration
- Mock API calls with MSW (Mock Service Worker) or vi.mock
- Test error states and loading states
- Snapshot tests only for stable UI components

## Data Consistency Tests (Critical for RAG)

- After document ingestion: verify chunk count in Qdrant matches expected
- Verify payload fields (document_id, content, filename, department) are populated
- Verify embedding dimensions match model output (384 for all-MiniLM-L6-v2)
- Verify PostgreSQL document status matches Qdrant state
- Verify query results return valid document_id references
- Verify deduplication: re-upload same file, assert no duplicate vectors
